# Category wildcards — auto-ignore any future private strategy/sales/pricing/VC docs
docs/*STRATEGY*.md
docs/*SALES*.md
docs/*PRICING*.md
docs/*GTM*.md
docs/*MRR*.md
docs/*VC*.md

# Internal session audits, phase reports, and dominance/roadmap speculation —
# facts-only self-review docs written during development, not public-facing
# product documentation. Keep this list in sync with what actually lands in
# docs/ each session rather than relying on a single broad wildcard.
docs/PHASE*.md
docs/V1_ENDGAME_RELEASE_DECISION.md
docs/V1_FINAL_RELEASE_AUDIT.md
docs/V1_SECURITY_RELEASE_REVIEW.md
docs/POST_V1_CODING_PLAN.md
docs/POST_V1_DOMINANCE_REVIEW.md
docs/BESA_FINAL_LEVEL_DOMINANCE_ARCHITECTURE.md
docs/REGULATORY_INEVITABILITY_MAP.md
docs/GATEGUARD_*.md
docs/ECC_GATEGUARD_ANALYSIS.md

# Personal research files that sometimes land in the repo root by accident
*.pdf

# Release notes are for GitHub Release copy-paste only — never committed
# (.tgz tarballs are already ignored above)
release-notes*.md

# Internal launch/marketing drafts — never committed to the public repo
LAUNCH_ASSETS.md

# Internal pricing and financial models. The docs/ patterns above only cover
# docs/ — these drafts land in the repo root, where a careless `git add -A`
# would publish them. Keep both locations covered.
PRICING_*.md
FINANCIAL_MODEL_*.md
FINANCIAL_MODEL_*.txt
